src/test/stress/README

Stress tests for CONCURRENTLY commands
======================================

This directory contains a test suite that stresses concurrent
operations that are expected to behave transparently to other sessions:
commands with a CONCURRENTLY option (REPACK, CREATE INDEX, REINDEX,
DROP INDEX, REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW, ALTER TABLE ... DETACH
PARTITION), logical replication apply racing with local modifications
on the subscriber, replication slot creation/removal, SERIALIZABLE
transactions racing with each other and with DDL, hot standbys
replaying such DDL while serving queries, crash recovery in the middle
of such commands, and VACUUM running alongside them.  The workloads
they run against include plain and bulk DML, COPY, upserts and MERGE
against unique indexes, foreign key checks, out-of-line (TOASTed)
values, cursors and cached plans held across the DDL, and partitioned
tables.  The
workloads run via pgbench against concurrently modified tables,
verifying invariants of the data and checking the resulting indexes
with the amcheck extension.  Any SQL error or broken invariant makes
pgbench abort (--exit-on-abort), failing the test.

The tests are not deterministic: they rely on timing and randomized
workloads to catch anomalies, so a passing run does not prove the
absence of bugs.  They are cheap enough to run by default, and their
duration can be scaled up for more thorough runs.

Duration scaling
================

The run time of each test is controlled by the stress_concurrently
value in PG_TEST_EXTRA:

    make check PG_TEST_EXTRA='stress_concurrently=10'

Each test file is calibrated so that a value of 1 makes it run for
about 6 seconds, and the increase should be roughly linear; a value of
0 disables the suite.  If PG_TEST_EXTRA does not mention
stress_concurrently at all, a value of 1 is assumed, except in
environments that declare themselves slow by setting
PG_TEST_TIMEOUT_DEFAULT (such as Valgrind buildfarm animals), where the
suite is skipped; use an explicit stress_concurrently value to override
that.

Shared helpers
==============

Boilerplate common to the tests -- deciding whether to run based on the
stress_concurrently value, and setting up a node with the usual
settings -- lives in t/StressConcurrently.pm.  Each test loads it with

    use FindBin;
    use lib $FindBin::RealBin;
    use StressConcurrently;

and calls stress_plan() and stress_init_node().  The workload each test
runs is spelled out inline, since that is what makes each test distinct.

Running the tests
=================

NOTE: You must have given the --enable-tap-tests argument to configure.

Run
    make check
or
    make installcheck
You can use "make installcheck" if you previously did "make install".
In that case, the code in the installation tree is tested.  With
"make check", a temporary installation tree is built from the current
sources and then tested.

See src/test/perl/README for more info about running these tests.
